# What Vercel does not need to receive to build the site.
#
# Everything committed here is uploaded to Vercel on every deployment and
# counts against Deployment Storage, so anything that is not a build input is
# worth naming. `.dockerignore` covers the same ground for the container build
# but Vercel does not read it, which is how ~59MB of art masters ended up
# travelling with every one of the ~10 deployments a day this repo makes.
#
# Only add a path here that `next build` genuinely never reads.

# The untouched original of every picture the app draws — ~59MB, and by design
# nothing serves or builds from them. See art-masters/README.md.
art-masters

# The native Android shell. Built by .github/workflows/android-release.yml,
# which wraps the already-deployed site rather than bundling one, so none of
# this is a web build input. `www` is the Capacitor webDir it fills in.
android
www

# Playwright specs and their fixtures: run by .github/workflows/e2e.yml against
# a deployment, never during one. `playwright.config.ts` names ./e2e as a
# string rather than importing it, so it stays type-checkable without them.
e2e

# Design docs and game design documents — read by people, not by the build.
docs
